Re: iTol, personally I would never look at source code that isn't OSI  
licensed, because of what's called tainting. If you end up writing  
code that just happens to mirror the code of a closed-source piece  
that you inspected, in theory and depending on the circumstances you  
can end up liable for copyright infringement. That's why I would not  
even want to see any code under an NDA or other closed-source  
agreement. (BTW iTol is Flash-based.)

